  <data name="Templates.RestorePoint.Name" xml:space="preserve"><value>Weekly System Restore Point</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.RestorePoint.Desc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Creates a named System Restore point once a week so you always have a recent rollback target.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.RestorePoint.Note" xml:space="preserve"><value>Requires administrator privileges and System Protection to be enabled.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.SystemScan.Name" xml:space="preserve"><value>System File Integrity Scan</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.SystemScan.Desc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Runs DISM component-store repair followed by System File Checker, writing the result to a log in your Documents folder.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.SystemScan.Note" xml:space="preserve"><value>Requires administrator privileges and can run for 15+ minutes.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.DnsFlush.Name" xml:space="preserve"><value>Flush DNS Cache at Logon</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.DnsFlush.Desc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Clears the DNS resolver cache when you sign in - useful when you switch networks or VPNs often.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.DnsFlush.Note" xml:space="preserve"><value>Requires administrator privileges.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.NodePrune.Name" xml:space="preserve"><value>npm / pnpm Cache Prune</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.NodePrune.Desc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Verifies and prunes the npm cache and removes stale pnpm store entries to reclaim several gigabytes.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.NodePrune.Note" xml:space="preserve"><value>Requires Node.js on PATH.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.ProjectBackup.Name" xml:space="preserve"><value>Nightly Project Folder Backup</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.ProjectBackup.Desc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Mirrors a project folder to a backup location with robocopy, skipping build output and dependency folders.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.ProjectBackup.Note" xml:space="preserve"><value>/MIR deletes files in the destination that no longer exist in the source. Check both paths first.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.DevServerRestart.Name" xml:space="preserve"><value>Restart a Windows Service Nightly</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.DevServerRestart.Desc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Restarts a long-running service (build agent, database, local server) to clear leaks. Change the service name before saving.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.DevServerRestart.Note" xml:space="preserve"><value>Requires administrator privileges. Replace 'MSSQLSERVER' with your own service name.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.DisplayOff.Name" xml:space="preserve"><value>Turn Off Displays on Lock</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.DisplayOff.Desc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Switches the monitors off as soon as you lock the workstation instead of waiting for the power timeout.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.DisplayOff.Note" xml:space="preserve"><value>Set the trigger's session state to "Lock" in the editor if it is not already.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.WeeklyReboot.Name" xml:space="preserve"><value>Weekly Restart when Idle</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.WeeklyReboot.Desc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Restarts the machine once a week during the night, but only while it is idle, to apply pending updates.</value></data>
  <data name="Templates.WeeklyReboot.Note" xml:space="preserve"><value>Restarts the machine. Unsaved work in open apps may be lost.</value></data>
